WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
Good to have you on Planetarian Daily Episode 97, it's June 21, 2026.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.300
Let's see what the latest research is telling us.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:15.680
The week's biggest developments pulled together what actually moved, why it matters, and what to watch next.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:22.140
An international team has produced the first complete connect home of an adult fruit fly nervous system.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.900
The wiring diagram covers every neuron connection in the brain and ventral nerve cord.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.640
Labs at Harvard Medical School and Princeton University led the project.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.160
The finished map now supports direct experiments on how individual circuits control behavior.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:46.060
University of Bristol researchers observed groups of dwarf mongooses altering their movement patterns in high risk zones.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:53.920
The animals also changed their communication and resource defense behaviors even without immediate rivals present.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:59.140
Adjustments scaled with the likelihood of conflict according to the observations.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:02.880
The study appears in nature ecology and evolution.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.920
Future work will test whether similar anticipation occurs in additional social species.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:12.020
Now shifting to a very different area of research.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:19.720
Plasma proteomic analysis has tracked biological age across more than 40 cell types from a single blood sample.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:26.860
Accelerated aging in specific cell populations correlated with elevated risk for particular diseases.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:33.320
The same approach also flagged individuals showing slower aging signatures in certain cell types.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.620
The method measures heterogeneous aging rates without needing separate tissue samples.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.060
Hundreds of wine grape seeds will orbit for approximately six months.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:48.280
The seeds received continuous cosmic radiation exposure before returned to Earth.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:55.840
After landing the seeds will be planted and grown to assess heritable changes in growth fruit chemistry and stress tolerance.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.160
The project aims to produce the first wine from space exposed grape lineages.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:09.100
Researchers expect the radiation dose to induce novel genetic variation not easily generated by terrestrial breeding.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:16.860
On a different note, childhood abuse or neglect has been linked to elevated mitochondrial respiratory capacity.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.800
That persists into adulthood.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:25.080
The increase appears driven by cellular stress adaptation rather than simple energy shortfalls.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:30.780
Researchers note the shift may help explain later differences in physical and mental health.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:36.720
Further longitudinal work is required to test whether the mitochondrial change can be reversed.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:45.540
A photonic platform at Southern University of Science and Technology captured five distinct phases of localization physics simultaneously.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:53.500
The setup used controlled disorder to track transitions that theorists had predicted but not previously measured together.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:59.100
Results indicate localization behavior is more varied than earlier models assumed.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.000
The team plans extensions to other quantum platforms to test generality.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:13.340
Next up, deletion of the SNF-1 gene in yeast shortens chronological lifespan under low glucose and amino acids.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:23.720
The same deletion lengthens lifespan and raises competitive fitness by roughly two orders of magnitude when glucose reaches 5% and amino acids are tripled.

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:28.200
The outcome parallels metabolic reprogramming seen in cancer cells.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.920
The work shows that one genetic change can produce opposite effects on aging depending on nutrient conditions.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:42.280
The chosen concept will examine how solar activity and atmospheric dynamics alter the near-earth space environment.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:48.320
Data are expected to improve forecasts for GPS accuracy and satellite operations.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:56.700
Shifting focus, advanced spectrometry has identified thousands of previously uncharacterized compounds in everyday foods.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:03.240
These molecules, described as nutritional dark matter, sit outside standard nutrient labels.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:08.260
Early data tie some of them to aging pathways and metabolic regulation.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:13.880
The mapping effort aims to rank which compounds deserve targeted human studies next.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:24.380
Analysis of U.S. suburban development since 1945 shows neighborhood design features explain more vehicle miles traveled than simple distance from city centers.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:32.400
Street patterns that force longer local trips and reduce walking account for a substantial share of household carbon output.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:38.620
The study reframes sprawl policy around street networks rather than density metrics alone.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:46.200
On another front, researchers have completed the first global map of fungal networks across terrestrial soils.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:53.920
The distribution data cover multiple ecosystems and establish a baseline for planetary scale below ground ecology.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:05:03.760
Southwest research institute measurements indicate the inner belt asteroid completes one end over end rotation every 10.5 earth days.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:08.040
It's spin axis wobbles every 25.5 days.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.740
The dual axis motion was revealed by Lucy data.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:21.940
Now moving to insect navigation, drone tracking of wild honey bees revealed that each individual maintains its own consistent flight route between foraging sites.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:28.120
Some paths repeated so precisely that bees passed within centimeters of earlier positions.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.900
Trees and other landmarks stabilize the roots while open fields increased variation.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:39.360
The observations show how insects rely on visual cues for precise navigation.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:51.000
University of Copenhagen economist track Danish firms facing low cost Chinese imports, while offshoring reduced local emissions, overall global emissions increased.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:57.740
The net rise occurred because production shifted to regions with higher carbon intensity per unit output.

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:02.580
The study used firm level data matched to trade and emissions records.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:08.200
Policy makers are examining whether carbon border adjustments could alter this pattern.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:17.660
Turning to technology, an AI system now operates optical tweezers that load, trap and measure hundreds of microscopic particles per hour.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:23.780
The closed loop platform removes manual steps from single particle biophysical assays.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:29.320
The method is already being applied to protein complexes and extracellular vesicles.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:38.280
Caltech researchers showed that stressed soil bacteria remodeled gene expression and metabolism to cope with phosphorus scarcity.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.660
The changes alter interactions with plant roots.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:48.600
Experiments combined controlled microcosms with transcriptomic profiling of bacterial communities.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:54.240
The findings matter for predicting ecosystem responses under nutrient limited conditions.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:07:02.780
Moving on, a high-resolution spatial proteomics atlas has mapped 13,000 proteins across human tissues.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:09.220
The atlas shows how protein organization varies by tissue context at cellular scale.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:14.700
It supplies a new reference for tracking disease-related changes, shifting topics.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:23.720
Nanobubbles roughly 100 nanometers across generate reactive species that degrade oil, algae and other water contaminants.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:29.420
The bubbles leave no chemical residues and remain suspended for extended periods.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:35.380
Field-scale tests are underway for municipal and agricultural water treatment systems.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:45.480
Next, AI analysis of prion proteins has identified short peptide sequences with potential activity against drug-resistant bacteria.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:50.000
The sequences could be repurposed for new antibiotic development.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:58.080
Finally, infectious disease researchers recorded an African origin virus transmitted by mosquitoes in Scottish samples.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:03.120
Heather Ferguson described the detection as unexpected within her career.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.320
The finding expands the known geographic range of the pathogen.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.280
Surveillance programs will monitor further northward spread.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:16.140
Keep an eye on results from expanded mosquito surveillance networks in northern Europe.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.560
